# Configuration for remarkable-web-stream.
#
#   cp tunnel.env.example tunnel.env     # tunnel.env is git-ignored
#
# deploy.sh copies tunnel.env to /home/root/rmshare/tunnel.env on the tablet
# (mode 600). It is read both by systemd (EnvironmentFile) and by
# run-tunnel.sh (sourced by /bin/sh), so keep values simple: no spaces,
# quotes, '$' or backslashes.

# --- Required -----------------------------------------------------------------

# Password viewers type into the login form (at least 8 characters).
# Use a long, random value: the page is reachable from the internet.
#   e.g. openssl rand -base64 18
RMSHARE_PASSWORD=change-me-to-something-long

# --- Tunnel mode (pick one; with nothing set, a Cloudflare quick tunnel is used) ---

# Tailscale Funnel: stable https://<TS_HOSTNAME>.<tailnet>.ts.net URL, free, no domain needed.
#TUNNEL=tailscale
#TS_HOSTNAME=remarkable
# Optional reusable auth key (admin console -> Settings -> Keys); without it the
# deploy prints a login link to approve the device.
#TS_AUTHKEY=tskey-auth-...

# Cloudflare named tunnel (requires a Cloudflare account and a domain).
#TUNNEL_TOKEN=eyJhIjoi...
# Shown on the /url page and in the document on the tablet.
#PUBLIC_URL=https://rm.example.com

# --- Optional -------------------------------------------------------------------

# Save a PDF with the current URL and a QR code to the tablet's library whenever
# the URL changes. Restarts xochitl (about 10 s) to make it show up. 1 = on, 0 = off.
#PUBLISH_DOC=1

# Quick/named Cloudflare tunnel watchdog: restart the tunnel after it has been
# "not ready" for this many seconds while the internet is reachable.
#TUNNEL_DEAD_AFTER=120
